# FTC Team <NNNNN> — BIOBUZZ 2026-27 Robot Code

## What this project is
Android Studio / Gradle fork of `FIRST-Tech-Challenge/FtcRobotController`.
Runs on a REV Control Hub (REV-31-1595). All of our code lives in `TeamCode/`.
Competition code must work with **no laptop connected** — see "Competition mode".
We are a <N>-student team. Time is our scarcest resource; correctness is our
scarcest quality. Prefer the smallest change that works.

## Pinned versions — never change these unless a human asks you to
- FTC SDK: **<11.2.1>** (declared in `build.dependencies.gradle`) — v11.2.1 released 2026-07-31
- Toolchain for SDK 11.2+: **Android Studio Narwhal 3 Feature Drop (2025.1.3) or later**,
  Gradle **9.1**, AGP **8.13.2**, JDK **17 or 21** · minSdk **24** · ABI `arm64-v8a`
  (The v11.2 release notes say the workspace *"requires Android Studio Narwhal 3 Feature Drop or
  later to build"*. The repo README's older "Ladybug (2024.2) or later" line and the ftc-docs
  "install JDK 17 separately" page both predate this. Do not downgrade Studio on their say-so.)
- Path library: <Pedro Pathing vX.Y.Z | Road Runner 1.0.x | none>
- Dashboard/telemetry tool: <FTC Dashboard 0.4.x | FTControl Panels vX.Y.Z> — **SHOP ONLY, see R704.D**
- Odometry: <goBILDA Pinpoint V2 3110-0002-0002 driver vX | SparkFun OTOS | drive encoders>
- Vision: <Limelight 3A firmware vX | SDK VisionPortal AprilTagProcessor | none>
- Other libs: <FTCLib vX.Y.Z | Sloth deploySloth vX.Y.Z | ...>

If you need an API that does not exist in these versions, **STOP and say so.**
Do not upgrade anything. Do not add a dependency. Both are human decisions.

## Build, deploy, logs — use exactly these commands
| Purpose | Command | You may run it? |
|---|---|---|
| Compile only (fast, no robot) | `./gradlew :TeamCode:compileDebugJavaWithJavac` | yes, freely |
| Unit tests (no robot) | `./gradlew :TeamCode:test` | yes, freely |
| Full build | `./gradlew :TeamCode:assembleDebug` | yes, freely |
| Install to robot | `./gradlew installDebug` | **ASK A HUMAN FIRST** |
| Hot reload TeamCode only | `./gradlew deploySloth` | **ASK A HUMAN FIRST** |
| Connect over robot Wi-Fi | `adb connect 192.168.43.1:5555` | ask |
| Pull the RC log | `adb pull /sdcard/robotControllerLog.txt logs/` | yes |

Compile and test are your feedback loop — use them constantly. **Anything that
changes what the physical machine does requires a human standing next to it.**

## NEVER modify these files or directories
- `FtcRobotController/**` — the SDK module. Read the ~200 sample OpModes for
  *reference only*. Never edit them. **Never imitate their structure**: the
  samples use blocking `sleep()` chains and inline magic numbers, both of which
  are banned below. If a compile error looks like it is "in the SDK", the bug is
  in `TeamCode/`.
- `libs/**`, `gradle/**`, `gradlew`, `gradlew.bat`, `settings.gradle`,
  `build.gradle`, `build.common.gradle`, `build.dependencies.gradle`,
  `gradle.properties`
- `.githooks/**`, `.claude/settings.json`

A permissions deny-rule and a pre-commit hook both enforce this. If you hit
either, that is the system working — report it, do not work around it, do not
suggest `--no-verify`.

